/* NOTE ( DPP_NonAdherence_BMI_ResetToPrior, EN )
>PARAMETER	Mode of BMI evolution when DPP adherence ceases
>LOCATION	Base(DPP_Intervention).dat
>LAST UPDATE	December 2015
>
>DESCRIPTION	When adherence to DPP ceases, this parameter tells POHEM to reset BMI
to value prior to DPP intervention (TRUE) or use current intervention value (FALSE).
Thereafter, the usual BMI equation takes over.
>DIMENSIONS	none
>SOURCE	
>
>DEFINITION	
>
>METHODS	Use this parameter to reset the BMI value after a person becomes
non-adherent to DPP intervention on BMI.  Set to TRUE to reset the BMI value 
at the level prior to the intervention before letting the BMI model take over 
(for rest of simulated life).  Set to FALSE to leave the BMI value at its
intervention level before letting the BMI model take over (for rest of simulated life).
>
>ASSUMPTIONS	
>
>DECISIONS	
>
>REFERENCES	
>
>RELATED PARAMETERS	
>
>COMMENTS

*/
/* NOTE ( DPP_gBMI, EN )
>PARAMETER	Minimum level of BMI (during year(s) for DPP program) to be a target
>LOCATION	Base(DPP_Intervention).dat
>LAST UPDATE	December 2015
>
>DESCRIPTION	This parameter defines the threshold value for BMI above which a
person may be defined to belong to the target population.
>DIMENSIONS	[SEX]
>SOURCE	This parameter has been introduced as a component of the criteria for
target population.
>
>DEFINITION	Threshold that BMI must reach or exceed so that a person may be
considered a target in year Year_for_DPP_program (if other criteria are
satisfied also).
>The complete criterion to define target population is:
>In Year_for_DPP_program (at birthday), the person must
>-	Be non-diabetic
>-	Have a BMI >= DPP_gBMI
>-	Have age within DppAgeRange
>-	Have 2-year probability of diabetes >=
Threshold_for_Elevated_Plasma_Glucose
>METHODS	-
>
>ASSUMPTIONS	Value in base scenario: 24.
>
>DECISIONS	The value chosen is the usual threshold used to define overweight or
obese persons.
>REFERENCES	None.
>RELATED PARAMETERS	DppAgeRange,
>Threshold_for_Elevated_Plasma_Glucose,
>Year_for_DPP_program
>COMMENTS
*/
