combined effect of intervention on PA and intervention on BMI will produce a
decrease of 7% of average BMI
>
>RELATED PARAMETERS	DPP_AdherenceBMI,
>DPP_Adherence_PA,
>DPP_proportion_shift_LTPA
>
*/
/* NOTE ( Threshold_for_Elevated_Plasma_Glucose, EN )
>PARAMETERS	DPoRT threshold for Elevated Plasma Glucose
>LOCATION	Base(DPP_Intervention).dat
>LAST UPDATE	December 2015
>
>DESCRIPTION	This parameter defines the threshold above which the 10-year
probability of diabetes must lie so that the person may be defined to belong to
the target population
>DIMENSIONS	[SEX][FROM_25_TO_80_BY_5]
>
>SOURCE	This parameter has been introduced as a component of the criteria for
target population.
>
>DEFINITION	Threshold that 10-year probability of diabetes must reach or exceed
so that a person may be considered a target in year Year_for_DPP_program (if
other criteria are satisfied also).
>The complete criterion to define target population is:
>In Year_for_DPP_program (at birthday), the person must
>-	Be non-diabetic
>-	Have a BMI >= DPP_gBMI
>-	Have age within DppAgeRange
>-	Have 2-year probability of diabetes >=
Threshold_for_Elevated_Plasma_Glucose
>
>METHODS	Analysis done in CHMS: a distribution of Elevated Plasma Glucose was
obtained using CHMS.  From this, percentage was defined for values above 5.3
and 6.1.  The parameter was then modified with small steps in successive
scenarios to determine values that give the percentages observed
>
>
>DECISIONS This was updated in June 2019 due to changes to DPoRT earlier in 2019 
and the use of 2 year risk rather than 10 year risk.
>RELATED PARAMETERS	DPP_gBMI,
>DppAgeRange,
>Year_for_DPP_program
*/
